    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0331" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg271"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Webb to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 65.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rio de Janeiro,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 25, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inclose the official
                    replies of “the allies” to my renewal of our tender of our “good offices.”
                    Circumstances beyond <pb facs="0332" n="272" xml:id="pg272"/> my control render
                    it impossible to furnish translations by this steamer, and therefore I forward
                    the original.</p>
                <p>“The allies” assume that the war in the river Plata is virtually at an end. The
                    future call upon them for men and money will be the best commentary upon the
                    accuracy of this assumption.</p>
                <p>Joáo Silviera de Souza has been appointed minister of foreign affairs, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">vice</hi> Albuquerque, deceased.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. WATSON WEBB.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




